{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter's New Job"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "First Contact"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 4}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Accurately use important information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le04ob04re1img01.png"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Connected Speech: Linking Sounds In Spoken English"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " In spoken English, sometimes you may have problems understanding what people are saying. This is not because you don't know the words being said or the person was speaking too fast, but because the words have been connected and the sounds changed. "}, {"type": "text", "content": " In English, native speakers tend to link the consonant at the end of a word with the vowel at the beginning of the following word. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "How ca<span class=\"underline\">n I</span> help you? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Ma<span class=\"underline\">y I</span> speak to Mr. Durham, please?  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Ca<span class=\"underline\">n I</span> put you on hold? "}, {"type": "example", "content": " I've go<span class=\"underline\">t it</span> all down. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Starting And Ending A Phone Conversation "}, {"type": "describer", "content": " Talking on the telephone can be challenging for a variety of reasons. Firstly, you are not able to see the person you're talking to, so there's no body language to be read. Secondly, it requires a special set of words, phrases, and expressions. "}, {"type": "text", "content": " The chart below will help you to speak on the phone confidently in business and personal situations. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Answering the phone</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Introducing yourself</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"underline\\\">For calls to your direct line</span> <span class=\\\"italic\\\"><ul><li>Good morning, this is Hannah.  <li>Good morning, Polygon firm. Hannah speaking. How can I help you?</li> <li>Farmani's office, Hannah speaking. </li></ul></span><br/>  <span class=\\\"underline\\\">For calls to a general number</span> <span class=\\\"italic\\\"><ul><li>Thank you for calling Polygon. How may I direct your call?</li></ul></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"underline\\\">When calling a general number</span> <span class=\\\"italic\\\"><ul><li>May I speak with Janet Ellison?</li> <li>Hello, this is Brianne Smith calling for Janet Ellison. </li> <li>Is Janet Ellison in?\\t</li></ul></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Connecting someone </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">When you don't understand the caller</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"underline\\\">When you answer the phone and it is for someone else</span> <span class=\\\"italic\\\"><ul><li>One minute, I'll transfer you.</li> <li>Please hold and I'll put you through. </li> <li>One moment, please.</li> <li>Just a moment. Can I put you on hold?</li></ul></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\"><ul><li>Could you please repeat that? <li>I'm sorry, I didn't catch that.</li> <li>I didn't catch what you just said. </li> <li>Can you speak a little more slowly?</li></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Taking a message for someone</span>  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Leaving a message for someone</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\"><ul><li>I'm sorry, Mark's not here at the moment. Can I take a message? </li> <li>He's in a meeting at the moment. May I ask who's calling?</li> <li>He's is busy at the moment. Would you like to leave a message?</li></ul></span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\"><ul><li>Please tell him that Janet called and ask him to call me back. My number is 555-325-5115.</li> <li>Could you tell him that Janet called?</li> <li>Please ask him to call Janet when he gets in.</li></ul></span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to put on hold"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make someone wait until the person they have called is ready to answer"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Can I put you on hold for a few minutes please?  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le04ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when speaking on the phone. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "take a call "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "speak to someone on the phone when someone else has answered "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He can't take your call at the moment. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le04ob04aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "in the middle of "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "busy doing something; busy with "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He is in the middle of a meeting. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le04ob04aud03"}], "typ